speechtext:
We have already a definition in our statutes. Perhaps that might be improved, but until it is improved it stands as the law of Canada. Section 2 of the 'Canadian Nationals Act reads:
The following persons are Canadian nationals, viz:
(a)	Any British subject who is a Canadian citizen within the meaning of the Immigration Act;
(b)	The wife of any such citizen;
(c)	Any person born out of Canada, whose father was a Canadian national at the time of that person's birth, or with regard to persons born before the third day of May, one thousand nine hundred and twenty-one, any person whose father at the time of such birth, possessed all the qualifications of a Canadian national, as defined in this act.
Under the Immigration Act, 1910, a Canadian citizen is defined as follows:
(b) "Canadian citizen" means
(i)	a person born in Canada who has not become an alien;
(ii)	a British subject who has Canadian domicile; or
(iii)	a person naturalized under the laws of Canada rvho has not subsequently become an alien or lost Canadian domicile:
Provided that for the purpose of this act a woman who has not been landed in Canada shall not be held to have acquired Canadian citizenship by virtue of her husband being a Canadian citizen; either shall a child who has not been landed in Canada be held to have acquired Canadian citizenship through its father or mother being a Canadian citizen;
That would be the definition of a Canadian national as referred to in this bill.

I move:
That section 19 of the said bill be amended by striking out the first eleven lines of the said section and substituting therefor the following:
"19. (1) The governor in council may, from time to time, by order or regulation provide for any or ail of the following matters:-
(a) the application of the provisions of this act, with necessary modifications, to any case in which there is a state of armed conflict, civil or otherwise, either within a foreign country or between foreign countries."
By striking out the letter (c) in line one on page six and substituting therefor the letter (b) ;
By striking out the letter (d) in line three on page six and substituting therefor the letter (c);
By striking out the letter (e) in line six and substituting therefor the letter (d);
By striking out the letter (f) in line eight and substituting therefor the letter (e).
